4	// grokfast_gfx942.hip.hpp — CANONICAL SuperGrok gfx942 step logic for 'grokfast'.
5	//
6	// AMDGCN-asm status (Stage 5 — AMD-native): this file now carries BOTH
7	//   (A) the ATen host orchestration (the public sg::gfx942::launch_grokfast_*
8	//       entry points the bindings call — UNCHANGED, byte-for-byte), AND
9	//   (B) a REAL hand-written AMDGCN grid-stride update kernel (§5 below) built
10	//       on the shared, compiler-verified primitives
11	//       csrc/backends/hip/gfx942/amdgcn_primitives.hip.hpp — streaming
12	//       (read-once) grad loads via amd::streaming_load and a streaming param
13	//       write-back via amd::streaming_store, fusing the EMA filter +
14	//       amplification + m/v EMAs + bias-corrected decoupled-weight-decay apply
15	//       into ONE kernel (vs the ATen path's chain of broadcast launches).
16	//
17	// COMPILE ROUTING (two passes, one header):
18	//   * HOST pass  (`!__AMDGCN__`): sees ONLY section (A) — torch + primitives +
19	//     the launchers; the thin host launch_grokfast.hip.cpp TU resolves unchanged.
20	//   * DEVICE pass (`__AMDGCN__` — scripts/amdgcn_check.sh — or `__HIPCC__`):
21	//     sees ONLY section (B), the device update kernel.
22	//
23	// ELEMENTWISE MATH: inlined (option a). The per-element step in
24	// csrc/algorithms/grokfast.h (grokfast_fused_step) pulls torch via
25	// csrc/common/*, which the bare amdgcn gate cannot resolve, so the ~10-line
26	// update is copied here verbatim (numerically identical: bc1/bc2 un-inverted →
27	// divide, sqrtf→__builtin_sqrtf).
28	//
29	// HARDWARE-GATED 🟡: device-compile-verified for gfx942 only; MI300X numeric
30	// parity vs the algorithm-header reference is deferred — see
31	// HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md, Stage 5.
32	//
33	// The production TU csrc/backends/hip/gfx942/launch_grokfast.hip.cpp now
34	// #include's this header and keeps only the host launcher(s) the pybind
35	// layer calls. Migrated byte-for-byte from that TU.
36	// ============================================================================
37	// HIP gfx942 launch glue for Grokfast.
38	// Algorithm: csrc/algorithms/grokfast.h
39	//
40	// COMPUTE PATTERN
41	// Identical to GrokAdamW (EMA amplification + AdamW). Hyperparameters differ;
42	// math is structurally the same.
43	//
44	// MFMA APPLICABILITY: none. Elementwise.
45	
46	// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
47	// (A) HOST orchestration — ATen public entry points. Compiled by the HOST pass
48	// only (torch/extension.h pulls in <cuda.h>/ATen, invisible to the bare device
49	// gate). Under hipcc (`#if __HIPCC__`) the host launcher now DISPATCHES the §5
50	// kernel via hipLaunchKernelGGL (see §5.LAUNCH); the `#else` branch keeps the
51	// ATen path as the CPU-host fallback.
52	// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
53	// SG_GFX942_DEVICE_TU (Stage 7): set by the thin `.hip` device TU so this host
54	// launcher is NOT re-emitted in that TU's host pass (it stays owned by the
55	// `.hip.cpp` host TU) — avoids a duplicate launch_grokfast_step at link.
56	#if !defined(__AMDGCN__) && !defined(SG_GFX942_DEVICE_TU)
